 "title": "Histone Methylation and Telomere Maintenance in Yeast and Drosophila",
 "summary": "This cluster is centered around histone methylation, a process that involves the gene or protein Sam1, which is also involved in stress granule assembly and colocalization with Sam2. Histone methylation is inhibited by SAH and SAHH, which accumulate in yeast and Drosophila. Telomere maintenance is also a key aspect, with Telomere having sequence homology with chr II and being involved in mmBIR. Drosophila is a model organism for histone methylation, and yeast has genomic locations on chr II and has an amplicon structure of SUL1. SAHH knockdown in Drosophila affects histone methylation.",
